{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your agent runs behind more than one server instance, or at the edge. A run\nspins up a sandbox, clones the repo, installs deps, does its work. The next run\nfor the same thread should pick that sandbox back up. Instead it builds a fresh\none every time and pays the whole cold-start cost again."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./lifecycle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle & Snapshots"}]},{"type":"text","value":" already knows how to resume, but its\nbookkeeping is in-memory, so it only holds within one process. The moment a run\nlands on a different replica (or a fresh isolate), that instance has never seen\nthe sandbox and re-creates it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sandbox instance durability"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is runtime placement, not chat history. It is\nowned by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-sandbox"},{"type":"text","value":", independent of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-persistence"},{"type":"text","value":"\n(transcript / runs / interrupts). You may share a database with chat stores, but\nyou compose a separate middleware."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Instance durability does not copy the workspace into your application storage.\nUse "},{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-configure","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep Files After Reload"}]},{"type":"text","value":" when a new\nsandbox must rebuild completed files, artifacts, and the saved conversation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is also not the agent's "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"output"}]},{"type":"text","value":". This page keeps a sandbox findable across\nprocesses; keeping the run's event stream readable across processes is\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./journal","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Run Journal"}]},{"type":"text","value":". The two compose: a resumed sandbox still holds the\njournal of every "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"durable"}]},{"type":"text","value":" run that executed in it, under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/tmp/tanstack-runs"},{"type":"text","value":".\n(Durable meaning "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":" was given both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runs"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"durability"},{"type":"text","value":". Journaling\nis opt-in, and a run without it leaves no file there.)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two pieces:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SandboxInstanceStore"}]},{"type":"text","value":": map of compound key → provider sandbox id (+\noptional snapshot). Durable, shared across instances."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LockStore"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai/locks"},{"type":"text","value":"): mutual exclusion around resume-or-create.\nMulti-instance needs a distributed lock. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/locks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Locks"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"wire-it-up","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wire it up"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hand the store to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":". The lock is a separate middleware because other\nmiddleware can share it, and it must come "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"before"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { InMemoryLockStore, withLocks } from '@tanstack/ai/locks'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport {\n  InMemorySandboxInstanceStore,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport type { ModelMessage } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\n// Single-process: in-memory is fine for local dev.\n// Multi-instance: your durable SandboxInstanceStore + distributed LockStore.\nconst instanceStore = new InMemorySandboxInstanceStore()\nconst messages: Array<ModelMessage> = [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }]\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'repo',\n  provider: {\n    name: 'example',\n    capabilities: () => ({\n      fs: true,\n      exec: true,\n      env: true,\n      ports: false,\n      backgroundProcesses: false,\n      writableStdin: false,\n      killableProcesses: false,\n      snapshots: false,\n      networkPolicy: false,\n      durableFilesystem: false,\n      fork: false,\n    }),\n    create: () => {\n      throw new Error('example provider: wire a real SandboxProvider')\n    },\n    resume: () => Promise.resolve(null),\n    destroy: () => Promise.resolve(),\n  },\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'none' } }),\n})\n\nchat({\n  adapter: grokBuildText('grok-build'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [\n    withLocks(new InMemoryLockStore()),\n    withSandbox(sandbox, { instances: instanceStore }),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reuse: 'thread'"},{"type":"text","value":" (the default), the first run creates and records the\ninstance. A later run for the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":" resumes it when the store (and\nlock) are shared across processes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Single sandbox, nothing else sharing the lock? Pass both as options and skip the\nextra middleware:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { InMemoryLockStore } from '@tanstack/ai/locks'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { instanceStore } from './instance-store'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nconst middleware = [\n  withSandbox(sandbox, {\n    instances: instanceStore,\n    locks: new InMemoryLockStore(), // multi-replica: a distributed LockStore\n  }),\n]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional chat persistence is independent:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { withLocks, InMemoryLockStore } from '@tanstack/ai/locks'\nimport { withPersistence, memoryPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { instanceStore } from './instance-store'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nconst middleware = [\n  withPersistence(memoryPersistence()), // chat state only\n  withLocks(new InMemoryLockStore()), // multi-replica: distributed LockStore\n  withSandbox(sandbox, { instances: instanceStore }),\n]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"implement-sandboxinstancestore","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Implement "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SandboxInstanceStore"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The store is three methods ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"upsert"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delete"},{"type":"text","value":"), each with an invariant that\na conformance suite checks for you.\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../persistence/build-a-sandbox-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build a Sandbox Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" walks through the\nimplementation, the table, and the suite, alongside the choice of how much a\nsandboxed run should leave behind at all."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"locks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Locks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A durable instance map without a distributed lock is still wrong across\nreplicas: two concurrent runs for one thread both find no record and both\ncreate. Pair the store with a lock, either "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withLocks"},{"type":"text","value":" from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai/locks"},{"type":"text","value":" or the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"locks"},{"type":"text","value":" option above. Full guide:\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/locks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Locks"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"see-also","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See also"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./journal","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Run Journal"}]},{"type":"text","value":": durability of a run's output, as opposed to its sandbox"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./takeover","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Takeover & Detached Runs"}]},{"type":"text","value":": surviving a client disconnect. A\ndetached run keeps its sandbox up, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunStore.sandboxKey"},{"type":"text","value":" /\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunStore.detachedSince"},{"type":"text","value":" is how a later host finds it again"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../persistence/build-a-sandbox-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build a Sandbox Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":": implement this store, and\nchoose how much a sandboxed run leaves behind"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/locks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Locks"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./lifecycle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../persistence/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persistence overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":": chat state only"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"wire-it-up","text":"Wire it up","level":2},{"id":"implement-sandboxinstancestore","text":"Implement SandboxInstanceStore","level":2},{"id":"locks","text":"Locks","level":2},{"id":"see-also","text":"See also","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYour agent runs behind more than one server instance, or at the edge. A run\nspins up a sandbox, clones the repo, installs deps, does its work. The next run\nfor the same thread should pick that sandbox back up. Instead it builds a fresh\none every time and pays the whole cold-start cost again.\n\n[Lifecycle & Snapshots](./lifecycle) already knows how to resume, but its\nbookkeeping is in-memory, so it only holds within one process. The moment a run\nlands on a different replica (or a fresh isolate), that instance has never seen\nthe sandbox and re-creates it.\n\n**Sandbox instance durability** is runtime placement, not chat history. It is\nowned by `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`, independent of `@tanstack/ai-persistence`\n(transcript / runs / interrupts). You may share a database with chat stores, but\nyou compose a separate middleware.\n\nInstance durability does not copy the workspace into your application storage.\nUse [Keep Files After Reload](./portable-snapshots-configure) when a new\nsandbox must rebuild completed files, artifacts, and the saved conversation.\n\nIt is also not the agent's *output*. This page keeps a sandbox findable across\nprocesses; keeping the run's event stream readable across processes is\n[The Run Journal](./journal). The two compose: a resumed sandbox still holds the\njournal of every **durable** run that executed in it, under `/tmp/tanstack-runs`.\n(Durable meaning `withSandbox` was given both `runs` and `durability`. Journaling\nis opt-in, and a run without it leaves no file there.)\n\nTwo pieces:\n\n- **`SandboxInstanceStore`**: map of compound key → provider sandbox id (+\n  optional snapshot). Durable, shared across instances.\n- **`LockStore`** (from `@tanstack/ai/locks`): mutual exclusion around resume-or-create.\n  Multi-instance needs a distributed lock. See [Locks](../advanced/locks).\n\n## Wire it up\n\nHand the store to `withSandbox`. The lock is a separate middleware because other\nmiddleware can share it, and it must come **before** `withSandbox`.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { InMemoryLockStore, withLocks } from '@tanstack/ai/locks'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport {\n  InMemorySandboxInstanceStore,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport type { ModelMessage } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\n// Single-process: in-memory is fine for local dev.\n// Multi-instance: your durable SandboxInstanceStore + distributed LockStore.\nconst instanceStore = new InMemorySandboxInstanceStore()\nconst messages: Array<ModelMessage> = [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }]\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'repo',\n  provider: {\n    name: 'example',\n    capabilities: () => ({\n      fs: true,\n      exec: true,\n      env: true,\n      ports: false,\n      backgroundProcesses: false,\n      writableStdin: false,\n      killableProcesses: false,\n      snapshots: false,\n      networkPolicy: false,\n      durableFilesystem: false,\n      fork: false,\n    }),\n    create: () => {\n      throw new Error('example provider: wire a real SandboxProvider')\n    },\n    resume: () => Promise.resolve(null),\n    destroy: () => Promise.resolve(),\n  },\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'none' } }),\n})\n\nchat({\n  adapter: grokBuildText('grok-build'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [\n    withLocks(new InMemoryLockStore()),\n    withSandbox(sandbox, { instances: instanceStore }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nWith `reuse: 'thread'` (the default), the first run creates and records the\ninstance. A later run for the same `threadId` resumes it when the store (and\nlock) are shared across processes.\n\nSingle sandbox, nothing else sharing the lock? Pass both as options and skip the\nextra middleware:\n\n```ts\nimport { InMemoryLockStore } from '@tanstack/ai/locks'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { instanceStore } from './instance-store'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nconst middleware = [\n  withSandbox(sandbox, {\n    instances: instanceStore,\n    locks: new InMemoryLockStore(), // multi-replica: a distributed LockStore\n  }),\n]\n```\n\nOptional chat persistence is independent:\n\n```ts\nimport { withLocks, InMemoryLockStore } from '@tanstack/ai/locks'\nimport { withPersistence, memoryPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { instanceStore } from './instance-store'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nconst middleware = [\n  withPersistence(memoryPersistence()), // chat state only\n  withLocks(new InMemoryLockStore()), // multi-replica: distributed LockStore\n  withSandbox(sandbox, { instances: instanceStore }),\n]\n```\n\n## Implement `SandboxInstanceStore`\n\nThe store is three methods (`get`, `upsert`, `delete`), each with an invariant that\na conformance suite checks for you.\n[Build a Sandbox Adapter](../persistence/build-a-sandbox-adapter) walks through the\nimplementation, the table, and the suite, alongside the choice of how much a\nsandboxed run should leave behind at all.\n\n## Locks\n\nA durable instance map without a distributed lock is still wrong across\nreplicas: two concurrent runs for one thread both find no record and both\ncreate. Pair the store with a lock, either `withLocks` from\n`@tanstack/ai/locks` or the `locks` option above. Full guide:\n[Locks](../advanced/locks).\n\n## See also\n\n- [The Run Journal](./journal): durability of a run's output, as opposed to its sandbox\n- [Takeover & Detached Runs](./takeover): surviving a client disconnect. A\n  detached run keeps its sandbox up, and `RunStore.sandboxKey` /\n  `RunStore.detachedSince` is how a later host finds it again\n- [Build a Sandbox Adapter](../persistence/build-a-sandbox-adapter): implement this store, and\n  choose how much a sandboxed run leaves behind\n- [Locks](../advanced/locks)\n- [Lifecycle](./lifecycle)\n- [Persistence overview](../persistence/overview): chat state only\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Sandbox Instance Durability\nid: sandbox-durability\norder: 9\ndescription: \"Durable sandbox instance resume across processes with a SandboxInstanceStore passed to withSandbox.\"\n---\n\nYour agent runs behind more than one server instance, or at the edge. A run\nspins up a sandbox, clones the repo, installs deps, does its work. The next run\nfor the same thread should pick that sandbox back up. Instead it builds a fresh\none every time and pays the whole cold-start cost again.\n\n[Lifecycle & Snapshots](./lifecycle) already knows how to resume, but its\nbookkeeping is in-memory, so it only holds within one process. The moment a run\nlands on a different replica (or a fresh isolate), that instance has never seen\nthe sandbox and re-creates it.\n\n**Sandbox instance durability** is runtime placement, not chat history. It is\nowned by `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`, independent of `@tanstack/ai-persistence`\n(transcript / runs / interrupts). You may share a database with chat stores, but\nyou compose a separate middleware.\n\nInstance durability does not copy the workspace into your application storage.\nUse [Keep Files After Reload](./portable-snapshots-configure) when a new\nsandbox must rebuild completed files, artifacts, and the saved conversation.\n\nIt is also not the agent's *output*. This page keeps a sandbox findable across\nprocesses; keeping the run's event stream readable across processes is\n[The Run Journal](./journal). The two compose: a resumed sandbox still holds the\njournal of every **durable** run that executed in it, under `/tmp/tanstack-runs`.\n(Durable meaning `withSandbox` was given both `runs` and `durability`. Journaling\nis opt-in, and a run without it leaves no file there.)\n\nTwo pieces:\n\n- **`SandboxInstanceStore`**: map of compound key → provider sandbox id (+\n  optional snapshot). Durable, shared across instances.\n- **`LockStore`** (from `@tanstack/ai/locks`): mutual exclusion around resume-or-create.\n  Multi-instance needs a distributed lock. See [Locks](../advanced/locks).\n\n## Wire it up\n\nHand the store to `withSandbox`. The lock is a separate middleware because other\nmiddleware can share it, and it must come **before** `withSandbox`.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { InMemoryLockStore, withLocks } from '@tanstack/ai/locks'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport {\n  InMemorySandboxInstanceStore,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport type { ModelMessage } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\n// Single-process: in-memory is fine for local dev.\n// Multi-instance: your durable SandboxInstanceStore + distributed LockStore.\nconst instanceStore = new InMemorySandboxInstanceStore()\nconst messages: Array<ModelMessage> = [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }]\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'repo',\n  provider: {\n    name: 'example',\n    capabilities: () => ({\n      fs: true,\n      exec: true,\n      env: true,\n      ports: false,\n      backgroundProcesses: false,\n      writableStdin: false,\n      killableProcesses: false,\n      snapshots: false,\n      networkPolicy: false,\n      durableFilesystem: false,\n      fork: false,\n    }),\n    create: () => {\n      throw new Error('example provider: wire a real SandboxProvider')\n    },\n    resume: () => Promise.resolve(null),\n    destroy: () => Promise.resolve(),\n  },\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({ source: { type: 'none' } }),\n})\n\nchat({\n  adapter: grokBuildText('grok-build'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [\n    withLocks(new InMemoryLockStore()),\n    withSandbox(sandbox, { instances: instanceStore }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nWith `reuse: 'thread'` (the default), the first run creates and records the\ninstance. A later run for the same `threadId` resumes it when the store (and\nlock) are shared across processes.\n\nSingle sandbox, nothing else sharing the lock? Pass both as options and skip the\nextra middleware:\n\n```ts\nimport { InMemoryLockStore } from '@tanstack/ai/locks'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { instanceStore } from './instance-store'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nconst middleware = [\n  withSandbox(sandbox, {\n    instances: instanceStore,\n    locks: new InMemoryLockStore(), // multi-replica: a distributed LockStore\n  }),\n]\n```\n\nOptional chat persistence is independent:\n\n```ts\nimport { withLocks, InMemoryLockStore } from '@tanstack/ai/locks'\nimport { withPersistence, memoryPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { instanceStore } from './instance-store'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nconst middleware = [\n  withPersistence(memoryPersistence()), // chat state only\n  withLocks(new InMemoryLockStore()), // multi-replica: distributed LockStore\n  withSandbox(sandbox, { instances: instanceStore }),\n]\n```\n\n## Implement `SandboxInstanceStore`\n\nThe store is three methods (`get`, `upsert`, `delete`), each with an invariant that\na conformance suite checks for you.\n[Build a Sandbox Adapter](../persistence/build-a-sandbox-adapter) walks through the\nimplementation, the table, and the suite, alongside the choice of how much a\nsandboxed run should leave behind at all.\n\n## Locks\n\nA durable instance map without a distributed lock is still wrong across\nreplicas: two concurrent runs for one thread both find no record and both\ncreate. Pair the store with a lock, either `withLocks` from\n`@tanstack/ai/locks` or the `locks` option above. Full guide:\n[Locks](../advanced/locks).\n\n## See also\n\n- [The Run Journal](./journal): durability of a run's output, as opposed to its sandbox\n- [Takeover & Detached Runs](./takeover): surviving a client disconnect. A\n  detached run keeps its sandbox up, and `RunStore.sandboxKey` /\n  `RunStore.detachedSince` is how a later host finds it again\n- [Build a Sandbox Adapter](../persistence/build-a-sandbox-adapter): implement this store, and\n  choose how much a sandboxed run leaves behind\n- [Locks](../advanced/locks)\n- [Lifecycle](./lifecycle)\n- [Persistence overview](../persistence/overview): chat state only\n"}
